WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.560
The tyrant, Sulyvahn, was only a young sorcerer when he left the painting.

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:14.120
Ariandel is another world; a sanctuary that pulls forlorn beings from the outside and gives them a home.

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:19.820
They find comfort in the sameness and they find comfort in the rot.

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:27.560
But imagine growing up in a place like this, surrounded by beings that have lost everything in the outside world

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:37.020
Sulyvahn, alone, had lost nothing so ironically, in this place of belonging he did not belong.

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:42.860
So it's no surprise that his envy inspired terrible ambition.

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:50.740
For, as Sulyvahn would prove, there's a lot to fear from a man with nothing to lose.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:58.440
So, a young sorcerer with spells of frost, he left and never returned.

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:05.020
"Where have you gone, sweet child? It's cold outside. It's awfully cold.

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:08.060
"Where have you run off to?"

00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:12.060
It was cold outside...home.

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:18.760
Far below a dark moon lies Anor Londo, City of the Gods.

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:23.760
Farther still, Irithyll, nestled in the Boreal Valley.

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:33.180
And yet, even farther below past the dungeon cells of Irithyll is the ruins of a once proud capital.

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:38.520
The only human kingdom to have ever been ruled by a Giant, actually.

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:48.460
But his story doesn't matter for he left nothing of worth behind...except perhaps, this: The Profaned Flame.

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:53.400
Profane, for it defies the law of fire and never goes out.

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:57.280
Profane, for it has the Abyss hidden within it.

00:01:57.980 --> 00:02:04.800
And Profane, for it corrupts the hearts of men, offering power but inspiring evil.

00:02:05.380 --> 00:02:10.320
Sulyvahn, items say, stumbled upon this place when he was yet a young sorcerer.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:16.500
It's not uncommon to see sorcerers out on distant journeys of discovery, and I bet

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:20.860
that when he left the capital, he was not the same man.

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:30.560
For from here on out, a burning ambition is said to have taken root within him and considering the nature

00:02:30.740 --> 00:02:34.900
of this flame, I think we can take that quite literally.

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:44.200
So with a greatsword, and perhaps a heart profaned by the flame, he left, his sights set on Irithyll.

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:51.100
For to Sulyvahn's dismay, this rotting world was just like the one he had left.

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:58.440
At this point in our story, Anor Londo was still a city of the old gods.

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:05.600
One of the most resilient cities in the world, for it and the old royalty who resided there,

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:10.620
remained largely unchanged throughout multiple links of fire.

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:13.960
It was home to the children of Gwyn himself.

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:16.920
Sister Gwynevere, with her Silver Knights.

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:24.660
Her brother Gwyndolin, captain of the Dark Moon Knights, and his half-sister Yorshka, the cross breed.

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:30.200
Power emanated from the cathedral, which was patrolled by the Silver Knights

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:35.380
and guarded by Ornstein and Smough, two famous knights of Gwyn.

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:43.200
The time would come, however, when Ornstein left the cathedral in search of Gwyn's first born child

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:49.760
making Smough the last knight to remain at his post, guarding the ruined cathedral.

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:58.480
There are also Deacons of the Way of White which have a sect here in Irithyll headed by Archdeacon McDonnell.

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:04.540
Far away, though, many more of this order toil in the Cathedral of the Deep,

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:08.860
devoted to maintaining the Age of Fire that Gwyn began.

00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:14.220
Here, great and terrible beings are put to their final rest.

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:21.600
And just now, in our story, a powerful saint named Aldrich has just been sacrificed to the First Flame,

00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:24.040
becoming a Lord of Cinder.

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:32.740
Back in Irithyll also, the order of the Darkmoon Knights led by the Dark Sun Gwyndolin swear their oaths.

00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:39.140
The blue phantoms are bound to become a shadow of Father Gwyn and a shadow of Sister Gwynevere,

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:45.120
hunting down any who would threaten the champions who link the fire.

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:53.440
And it was this order, the Darkmoon Knights, that the sorcerer Sulyvahn saw fit to infiltrate.

00:04:53.800 --> 00:04:58.620
And we know this because he was presented with the Greatsword of Judgement,

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:02.780
a ceremonial sword representing the judgement of the moon.

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:07.880
It glows like the blue of the Darkmoon, but much deeper.

00:05:08.380 --> 00:05:14.200
If you were to look more closely at this blade, then you would realize that its magic is

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:18.480
far closer to sorcery than any existing Lunar power.

00:05:18.980 --> 00:05:25.300
For Sulyvahn did not draw his power from faith like the other knights did,

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:32.320
but he drew it, instead, from sorcery which is an art that is despised by the old royalty.

00:05:32.740 --> 00:05:41.000
And, perhaps that's for good reason, for sorcery would ultimately be the downfall of the Way of White,

00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:44.580
the Darkmoon Knights, and the Gods alike.

00:05:45.340 --> 00:05:48.640
When the old world is rotten, you burn it away.

00:05:48.920 --> 00:05:55.500
And so the Pontiff's usurpation of Anor Londo began with Gwyndolin.

00:05:56.520 --> 00:06:02.700
"The Darkmoon Knights were once led by my elder brother, The Dark Sun Gwyndolin.

00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:08.920
"But he was stricken by illness and leadership of the knights fell to me.

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:16.080
"Then, Sulyvahn wrongfully proclaimed himself Pontiff and took me prisoner.

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:20.380
"Oh where could my dear brother be?"

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:29.360
Yorshka, the last remaining Knightess of the Darkmoon Order, mentions that it all began when her brother fell ill.

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:36.660
She doesn't blame his illness on Sulyvahn, but you and I both know that either he or his subordinates

00:06:37.060 --> 00:06:45.180
weren't above using poison, for it was not only the Darkmoon Knights affected by Sulyvahn's influence.

00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:49.900
The Holy Deacons also were befouled from within.

00:06:50.540 --> 00:06:59.180
Archdeacon McDonnell, a prominent member of their order who resides in Irithyll, committed a grave trespass.

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:06.300
He began to channel his faith for sorcery, transforming symbols of ecclesiastic authority

00:07:06.460 --> 00:07:09.960
into catalysts of Deep soul sorceries.

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:16.000
For McDonnell these stagnating souls and the magic derived from them

00:07:16.180 --> 00:07:19.780
represented the glorious bedrock of this world.

00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:25.320
Their order was intended to deal with the great and terrible beings that came

00:07:25.320 --> 00:07:30.960
to them, but inevitably they were affected by the terrors that came into the cathedral.

00:07:31.540 --> 00:07:34.560
This treason was not kept within Irithyll.

00:07:34.940 --> 00:07:41.020
No, McDonnell also imparted Deep soul sorceries to Archdeacon Royce

00:07:41.140 --> 00:07:44.640
and his Deacons who all resided in the cathedral.

00:07:44.920 --> 00:07:48.920
And he added new dark pages to their tome of miracles.

00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:55.360
Literally corrupting his order against the very flame that they had sworn to protect.

00:07:55.840 --> 00:08:01.480
He was undoubtedly collaborating with the sorcerer Sulyvahn who himself

00:08:01.480 --> 00:08:05.760
had his new knights infected and empowered by the Deep.

00:08:06.180 --> 00:08:10.640
Dark magics erupt from their throats, drawn towards life and

00:08:10.640 --> 00:08:18.380
their very weapons became eaten away by the tiny, biting insects that feed upon those close to the Deep.

00:08:18.660 --> 00:08:25.140
This force in Irithyll wielding the Profaned Flame, gnawed at by the Deep, headed by the

00:08:25.140 --> 00:08:33.460
Archdeacons and the Pontiff became an evil that pushed the entire royal family out of their ancient home.

00:08:34.060 --> 00:08:38.960
However, some residents clearly escaped all of this trauma.

00:08:39.400 --> 00:08:45.000
Because later, far away in a city named Lothric,  it is said

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:52.760
that there is another queen revered as a goddess  of fertility and bounty, just like Gwynevere once was.

00:08:53.360 --> 00:09:01.080
But back in Anor Londo, now with Pontiff Sulyvahn fully in control, the true atrocities could begin.

00:09:02.200 --> 00:09:10.420
Many in Irithyll were enslaved and as you can see, were pushed forward as fodder by the Pontiff's Fire Witches.

00:09:10.700 --> 00:09:13.880
The less fortunate were turned into beasts.

00:09:14.120 --> 00:09:21.060
For it is said that men who peer into the black eyes of Sulyvahn are transformed.

00:09:21.300 --> 00:09:24.580
Look closely at the faces of the dogs,

00:09:24.800 --> 00:09:26.920
at the hair of the spider women,

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:32.020
at these rib cage beasts that pray when they're defenseless.

00:09:32.300 --> 00:09:39.880
Sulyvahn forced out the beasthood within men, especially in those who would become his Outrider Knights.

00:09:40.960 --> 00:09:46.200
The most notable of the Outrider Knights was the Dancer of the Boreal Valley.

00:09:46.540 --> 00:09:51.480
Her Aurora Veil is actually an artifact of the old gods.

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:57.080
Permitted only to be worn by direct descendants of the old royal family.

00:09:57.480 --> 00:10:04.580
And before she was controlled by Sulyvahn, the Dancer was likely a daughter of Gwynevere,

00:10:04.780 --> 00:10:08.300
as she has a fragment of her mother's soul

00:10:08.640 --> 00:10:14.400
However, she was clearly left behind as the rest of her family escaped to Lothric.

00:10:14.800 --> 00:10:22.200
When captured, the Pontiff ordered her to serve first as a dancer, perhaps to shame her or entertain him.

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:30.100
Then, he made her an Outrider Knight, giving her a ring of his right eye that he knew would transform her.

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:33.880
She became an...enchanting beast of death.

00:10:34.160 --> 00:10:37.000
Her armor fusing with her own hide.

00:10:37.880 --> 00:10:45.260
Never far from the fleeting Dancer was Vordt, the Outrider Knight who received the Pontiff's Left Eye ring.

00:10:45.820 --> 00:10:48.400
Clearly, there was something between them.

00:10:48.680 --> 00:10:53.580
Some bond shared, for they would never return to Irithyll, but

00:10:54.060 --> 00:11:01.560
like all the Outrider Knights, their spirits can sometimes been seen roaming the old city...together.

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:06.900
In total, five Outrider Knights were dispatched to Lothric.

00:11:07.300 --> 00:11:09.900
One guarding the Road of Sacrifices.

00:11:10.220 --> 00:11:13.040
The second, in the basement of Lothric Castle.

00:11:13.580 --> 00:11:16.420
The third, skulking in the Grand Archives.

00:11:16.760 --> 00:11:25.900
And the two most unique knights, Vordt and the Dancer, guard the main exit and entrace to Lothric Castle itself.

00:11:26.280 --> 00:11:28.060
Their placement is no coincidence.

00:11:28.260 --> 00:11:33.460
Sulyvahn may be back in Irithyll, but he knows that the last vestiges of the royal family

00:11:33.520 --> 00:11:38.820
have a presence in Lothric, and his eyes are all over their failing kingdom.

00:11:39.340 --> 00:11:46.600
Watching, as the royal family desperately struggles to produce an heir to the linking of the fire.

00:11:47.060 --> 00:11:54.900
Waiting, as he knows that when they fail, Aldrich will be raised once more as a Lord of Cinder.

00:11:55.780 --> 00:12:00.600
And who do you think he'll be indebted to when he rises from his grave?

00:12:01.760 --> 00:12:07.880
To this end, Sulyvahn protected the gate to Irithyll with an old trick from the Painted World.

00:12:08.340 --> 00:12:16.500
A magical barrier was erected, repelling everything and everyone except those with a message from a small doll.

00:12:16.840 --> 00:12:21.340
"Wherever you go," it says, "the moon still sets in Irithyll.

00:12:21.720 --> 00:12:25.300
"Wherever you may be, Irithyll is your home."

00:12:25.820 --> 00:12:32.600
Sulyvahn, or the Deacons, placed one of these dolls in Aldrich's coffin and waited.

00:12:33.260 --> 00:12:38.400
And eventually, of course, he came for where else would he go?

00:12:39.820 --> 00:12:44.720
Aldrich had spent a long time ruminating on the fading of the fire.

00:12:45.160 --> 00:12:52.600
For him, it inspired prophetic visions of a new future, an age not of fire, but of deep seas.

00:12:53.080 --> 00:12:58.040
He knew the path to this world would be arduous, but he had no fear,

00:12:58.200 --> 00:13:04.060
for he would become not a mere devourer of men, but a devourer of gods.

00:13:04.380 --> 00:13:10.820
And so, imagine his pleasure when he found one waiting for him in his new cathedral.

00:13:11.620 --> 00:13:17.180
Gwyndolin, son of Gwyn and former captain of the Darkmoon Knights.

00:13:17.960 --> 00:13:27.040
"If only he were here, I would be most pleased for you both to meet; as, most assuredly, would he."

00:13:28.020 --> 00:13:30.880
But Aldrich wasn't the only being resurrected.

00:13:31.440 --> 00:13:37.400
You put the Pontiff's achievements to shame, rolling over him with the help

00:13:37.420 --> 00:13:46.020
of either Blackhand Gotthard for Lothric, the Pale Shade for Londor, or Anri for Horace.

00:13:46.480 --> 00:13:52.360
The Pontiff made many enemies, and they were his downfall in the end.

00:13:53.120 --> 00:13:57.200
Here you have a man who stopped at nothing to change the world.

00:13:57.460 --> 00:14:01.240
He mastered sorceries of frost, miracles of the moon,

00:14:01.620 --> 00:14:07.700
he partnered with a kingdom ending flame, and took advantage of the Deep.

00:14:08.440 --> 00:14:16.520
He used all of this plus social and political manipulation to usurp an age old kingdom, rising within the ranks

00:14:16.520 --> 00:14:24.200
of its knights, twisting its Deacons to feed a god to a Lord of Cinder and supplant the age of fire.

00:14:24.700 --> 00:14:31.540
The tyrant, Sulyvahn, tore apart many bonds but was undone himself by a mere Unkindled.

00:14:32.100 --> 00:14:37.900
Proof that no champion is more powerful than the fire linking curse.

00:14:38.960 --> 00:14:43.980
So if this man can't change the world, then what hope do we have?

